{"name":"Nutmeg Frost","hex":"#ecd9ca","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"nutmeg","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An evergreen tree (Myristica fragrans) cultivated in the East Indies for its spicy seeds.","The aromatic seed of this tree, used as a spice.\n The powdered seed, ready for use.\n A whole nutmeg seed."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To flavour with nutmeg.","To play the ball between the legs of (an opponent)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nutmeg"},{"term":"frost","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A cover of minute ice crystals on objects that are exposed to the air. Frost is formed by the same process as dew, except that the temperature of the frosted object is below freezing.","The cold weather that causes these ice crystals to form."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To cover with frost.","To become covered with frost."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/frost"}],"entries":[{"title":"Nutmeg","blocks":[{"text":"Nutmeg is the seed, or the ground spice derived from the seed, of several tree species of the genus Myristica; fragrant nutmeg or true nutmeg is a dark-leaved evergreen tree cultivated for two spices derived from its fruit: nutmeg, from its seed, and mace, from the seed covering. It is also a commercial source of nutmeg essential oil and nutmeg butter. The Banda Islands, in Maluku, Indonesia, are the main producer of nutmeg and mace, and the true nutmeg tree is native to the islands."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c8/Biji_Pala_Bubuk.jpg/330px-Biji_Pala_Bubuk.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nutmeg","wikidata":"Q83165"},{"title":"Frost","blocks":[{"text":"Frost is a layer of ice on a solid surface, which forms from water vapor that deposits onto a freezing surface. Frost forms when the air contains more water vapor than it can normally hold at a specific 